From 064e26445ea776205dade96d203024dc43d0b775 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:24:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Add the H713's LSB-aligned P010 (PL10)

The H713 AV1 core writes 10-bit frames in P010's layout with each sample in
bits 9:0 of its 16-bit word; it cannot MSB-align them. The local kernel
names that V4L2_PIX_FMT_P010_LSB ('PL10') on the capture queue and
DRM_FORMAT_P010 + DRM_FORMAT_MOD_ALLWINNER_LSB10 for scanout, and it is the
only 10-bit format the core offers, so without an entry 10-bit AV1 failed
with "failed to select a CAPTURE format".

The surfaces stay VA P010. Exports say P010 + LSB10, truthfully. A
mapping would hand LSB samples out as P010, so DeriveImage refuses it and
the copying paths shift into place (<<6 on GetImage, >>6 on PutImage).

hbd720 10/10 and hbd720-long 300/300 frames bit-exact against libdav1d.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Origin: https://github.com/cstenger/allwinner-h713-mainline/blob/43b2cdd4aa1b161a281db8b10f02ce70085e2d42/patches/libva-v4l2_request/0002-Add-the-H713-s-LSB-aligned-P010-PL10.patch (0002-Add-the-H713-s-LSB-aligned-P010-PL10.patch, commit ae94ce3)
